  "description": "portfolio-admin is a production-grade software engineering system implemented primarily in JavaScript, TypeScript. and structured persistence powered by MongoDB.\n\nSystem Architecture & Component Topology: The core application is partitioned into clear service boundaries. Backend request processing is powered by Express, WebSockets, managing incoming payload validation, CORS policies, and rate-limiting middleware. The user presentation layer is built using React, TailwindCSS, utilizing reactive component hierarchies and state management. The codebase is structured modularly across key functional boundaries including Server (server), Controllers (server/controllers), Models (server/models), Routes (server/routes), Services (src/services), Utils (src/utils), Src (src), Components (src/pages/studio/tools/pdf/components), Lib (src/lib), Pages (src/pages).\n\nData Pipeline & Execution Lifecycle: Incoming requests follow a deterministic lifecycle. The network interface exposes 94 primary REST/WebSocket routes including GET /, GET /:id, POST /, PUT /:id. Requests enter through designated entrypoint routes, pass through authentication and parameter validation, and execute business logic within isolated service modules. Output data frames and JSON models are serialized cleanly back to callers.\n\nInfrastructure, Reliability & Build System: Environment variables are managed using isolated configuration templates. Automated linting, static analysis, and code quality checks are enforced via TypeScript, ESLint.\n\nProject Background & Documentation: Portfolio Admin Panel - Backend Server Complete MVC backend server with MongoDB and Express. ## Features - **Authentication**: JWT-based authentication system - **CRUD Operations**: Complete CRUD for all entities - **Image Workflow**: Store public image URLs directly in MongoDB - **RESTful API**: Clean and organized REST API endpoints - **Security**: Protected routes with JWT middleware - **MVC Architecture**: Models, Controllers, and Routes separation │ ├── db.js # Mon",
